The following parts of Godbot incorporate and adapt that work:

- src/client/team-ui/ originates in ds-bot/src/client/ and its shared
  utilities. Godbot integrates workspace navigation, session selection,
  schedules, provider accounts, diagnostics, terminal controls and its
  visual identity directly in the source modules. The team UI uses CLI
  vendor marks. The original notices identify
  the trademark owners and Simple Icons (CC0) contributions.
- src/host/team-runtime/ includes modules from ds-bot/index.js,
  ds-bot/src/{host,shared,office}/, the web search provider and the
  distributed phone link. Godbot adapts the service and storage namespaces,
  workspace ownership, web and native session control, provider accounts,
  connectors, browser environments and the team roster.
- src/link/ is ds-bot's link/src (the phone link shared by the phone app and
  the computer, which itself adapts DSH Remote's MIT connection code; see the
  original notices). Godbot changed the pairing scheme to godbot:// (dsbot://
  still parses) and added the push extension: the push.register, push.send and
  push.result frames, the push.fcm.v1 capability, HostLink.sendPush,
  RelayTransport.registerPush and the end-to-end encrypted notifications in
  push.ts. src/host/team-runtime/mobile-link.js is built from it by
  scripts/build-link.mjs.
- src/drivers/external/{acp,claude,codex,discover,engines,jsonrpc,mcp-stdio}.js
  and src/team/mcp.js originate in ds-bot/src/host/local-agents/.
  Godbot adapts protocol handling, request correlation, team tools and
  native turn outcomes. src/team/mentions.js originates in
  ds-bot/src/shared/mentions.js.
- test/external/local-agents-*.test.js, protocol fixtures, Windows shims,
  recorded upstream samples and test/team-runtime/fake-ctx.js incorporate
  tests and samples from ds-bot/test/. Godbot's native qualification
  results and packaged integration runs are recorded separately.

The original notices also identify dependencies bundled in the phone link
and provide attribution for Office skills, artwork and other components.

